    "text": {
     "en": "The heart pumps blood round the body through tubes called blood vessels. Blood carries oxygen and digested food to every cell and takes away waste.\nArteries carry blood away from the heart and veins bring it back. Capillaries are tiny vessels where exchange happens.\nThe heart beats about 72 times a minute at rest and faster during exercise."
    }
